input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI is like having a small, smart computer that runs AI tasks right on your phone, tablet, or wearable device, instead of sending data to the internet or a server. Imagine a calculator that can recognize objects in real time, like a camera in your phone that instantly detects what's in front of you. This AI works locally, so it's faster and keeps your data private. It's like having a tiny brain that helps you do smart things without needing to connect to the web.

